soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: reopen the call path when the park does not take

The park closes the call path before it writes the reset and the clock:
cpu_comm_parked_since set, mips_app_ready_assumed cleared, the ioctl
suspend count raised. When either register does not read back 0 the late
suspend fails with -EIO. The PM core then resumes only the devices whose
late suspend succeeded, so resume_early never ran for cpu_comm, and the
awake system kept refusing every kernel call with -ENODEV and every RPC
ioctl with -EFAULT until a reboot, while the MIPS, whose reset write is the
one that may not have taken, could still be running. The error line did
not say that.

On that path the driver now clears the flag and restores the assumption
under the call mutex, drops the ioctl suspend count again, and says in
the error line that the standby is refused and calls are open again.
Whether the coprocessor still runs is left open there; the two values
read back show which write did not take. The next suspend to RAM parks
again if the MIPS status still reads "running".

Not measured; the read-back itself has not run on the device yet.
Compiled out of tree with W=1, no new warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -2210,6 +2210,7 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 {
 	void __iomem *ccu;
 	u32 rst, clk;
+	int assumed;
 
 	/*
 	 * Only for standby to RAM, where the DRAM goes into self-refresh. On
@@ -2234,6 +2235,7 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 	 */
 	mutex_lock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
 	WRITE_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since, cpu_comm_s2r_count);
+	assumed = mips_app_ready_assumed;
 	mips_app_ready_assumed = 0;
 	mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
 
@@ -2246,8 +2248,18 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 	clk = readl(ccu);
 	iounmap(ccu);
 	if (rst || clk) {
-		pr_err("cpu_comm: standby: park did not take (reset %08x, clock %08x)\n",
-		       rst, clk);
+		/*
+		 * The suspend fails, and no resume_early follows for this
+		 * device: reopen what the park closed, or the awake system
+		 * keeps refusing every call until a reboot.
+		 */
+		mutex_lock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
+		WRITE_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since, 0);
+		mips_app_ready_assumed = assumed;
+		mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
+		cpu_comm_resume(0);
+		pr_err("cpu_comm: suspend-to-RAM #%u refused: park did not take (reset %08x, clock %08x), calls and ioctls open again, coprocessor state unknown\n",
+		       cpu_comm_s2r_count, rst, clk);
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 	pr_info("cpu_comm: suspend-to-RAM #%u: coprocessor parked, kernel RPCs fail with -ENODEV and ioctl RPCs with -EFAULT until it is reloaded\n",
